The tool rejected my structured output three times with "must have required property 'finished'", even though I supplied that field. So the answer below is the JSON in the required schema, given as text.

```json
{
  "summary": "P1 galerie furnished in parts/room-6.mjs: a rocker, a bench, a side table with a lamp and a pot, and a floor lantern on the deck. Two hanging lanterns place once the roof exists. make.sh writes a whole build.nbt; this part shows no REFUSED or OFF-PALETTE lines.",
  "waste": [
    {
      "what": "Lantern spots and refused writes were found by re-running make.sh and the room check several times. The hanging-lantern failure showed only as an unexplained 'placed' count.",
      "cost": "about 4 make and check cycles, roughly 3 minutes",
      "tool": "`mcd room` could report refused writes per room with the reason (for example 'no ceiling'), so the cause shows at once."
    },
    {
      "what": "The door-front and shutter cells on z9 (x15..22) were worked out by hand from the plan's FACADES text.",
      "cost": "coordinate reasoning, about 2 minutes",
      "tool": "A per-room list of reserved and keep-clear cells in plan.md would give the lane and door fronts directly."
    }
  ],
  "companions": [
    {
      "role": "lamplighter",
      "task": "Confirm the hanging lantern spots at (16,5,8) and (18,5,8) once the roof underside exists, and check that the west corner reads as a porch lantern rather than a floor lamp."
    },
    {
      "role": "stair joiner",
      "task": "Check that the steps x17..18 z6 and the French doors x16..17 and x20..21 connect to the lane through the clear door fronts, so the walk verdict says OK in the full build."
    }
  ],
  "finished": true,
  "left": [
    "The walk verdict is UNREACHABLE in this stub build because the steps (x17..18 z6) and the French doors (z10) belong to other parts. Re-run `$MCD room` in the full build to confirm the lane x17..18 and the door fronts x16/17/20/21 z9 connect.",
    "The hanging lanterns at (16,5,8) and (18,5,8) were refused here because there is no roof underside yet. They should place once the roof is laid; light is 10+ without them.",
    "Only one rocker: it is a plain dark_oak_stairs seat with no trapdoor back, because the back cell at z9 is a shutter or a door front. x15 z8 is a floor lantern for the west corner instead of a second rocker.",
    "The shutters at z9 x15/18/19/22 and the posts and rail on z7 are fittings' cells and were not touched."
  ]
}
```

Notes on the build:
- Floor light is 10 to 15 on every cell (0 dark, 0 dim) with only the placed lanterns.
- The room check's FIT line is OK for this room.
- The room render from above (`room.png`) reads as a gallery with the bench, rocker, side table and lamp; the roof is not yet in the stub build, so the view is open.
- I added a note to plan.md's Notes with the galerie's layout constraints.
